   {:language :lean4
    :api "Mathlib `ContDiff` over the current `WithTop ℕ∞` smoothness index"}
   :trap
   "`ContDiff ℝ ⊤ f` does not mean infinitely differentiable. Here `⊤ = ω` requires real analyticity, strictly above the smooth index `∞`."
   :consequence
   "A quantifier over compactly supported `ContDiff ℝ ⊤` functions on `ℝ` is vacuous: the real-analytic identity theorem forces every such function to be identically zero."
